Error: Jet.RouteMethodTokenRefused: HTTPRouter custom route method must be a static String
  --> run.jet:7:24
    |
  7 |     print(table.custom(method, "/cache", "purge"))
    |                        ^^^^^^
 Why: Router and `#Server.Custom` routes are fully checked while building; only an App takes a run-time method, checked when it registers
 Fix: Use a literal or compile-time String constant, or register the route on a `web.app()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.RouteMethodTokenRefused

Error: Jet.InvalidRoute: Invalid HTTP route `/users/{id}`: brace interpolation is not allowed in route patterns
  --> run.jet:13:21
    |
 13 |     print(table.get("/users/{id}", "show"))
    |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: Route patterns use one canonical grammar; ambiguous escapes, traversal, duplicate names, and retired markers would make routing and audit metadata disagree
 Fix: Use `:name` for one segment or final `*name` for a catch-all; percent-encode a literal leading `:` or `*`, and never encode `/`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InvalidRoute

Error: Jet.AmbiguousRoute: Two routes both match `GET /a/:name`.
  --> run.jet:15:17
    |
 15 |     print(table.get("/a/:name", "b"))
    |                 ^^^
  --> run.jet:14:17
    |
 14 |     print(table.get("/a/:id", "a"))
    |                 ^^^ first registered here
 Why: Pages, convention files, handler routes and marked methods share one route table, so two rows with one method and address make dispatch ambiguous and one of them would never be reached. A route added while the program runs is checked when it is added.
 Fix: Remove one of the two registrations, rename the convention file, or make the addresses distinct (e.g. mount one under its own prefix).
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.AmbiguousRoute

Error: Jet.ExpiringForce: `ExpiringValue.force` bypasses expiry checking
  --> run.jet:18:17
    |
 18 |     print(lease.force())
    |                 ^^^^^
 Why: TTL-wrapped values must use fallible `get(clock)` so expired access is handled explicitly
 Fix: Use `.get(clock)` and handle `Expired`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.ExpiringForce

